      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1291892841,
      "text": "Dioscorea dumetorum, also known as the bitter yam, cluster yam, trifoliate yam, or three-leaved yam, is a species of flowering plant in the yam family, Dioscorea. It is native to sub-Saharan Africa and especially common in the tropical regions of West Africa, including Nigeria, Benin, and Ghana. D. dumetorum has both toxic and non-toxic varieties."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Dioscorea dumetorum",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dioscorea_dumetorum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 207971513,
      "text": "Dioscorea dumetorum, l'igname amère ou igname trifoliée, est une espèce de plantes monocotylédones de la famille des Dioscoreaceae, originaire de l'Afrique tropicale."
    }
